(7438509, 1175738, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>hey Marcel!  I don''t mind the image or your concept, but sadly it misses the mark in terms of interpretation of what the challenge called for. The composition is ok with the arms coming in from the sides and making a centred high-5, and I can see you kept things simple and didn''t try to do too much with the concept.  Some voters might have disliked the shadow cast by the hands; if possible, try to position models about 3ft away from your backdrop.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! hey Marcel!  I don''t mind the image or your concept, but sadly it misses the mark in terms of interpretation of what the challenge called for. The composition is ok with the arms coming in from the sides and making a centred high-5, and I can see you kept things simple and didn''t try to do too much with the concept.  Some voters might have disliked the shadow cast by the hands; if possible, try to position models about 3ft away from your backdrop. Keep up the good work! Susan', '2016-02-20 21:09:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7438510, 1175533, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>What, those things can <i>run?</i> Never would have guessed it, but bet it can dig like hell with those claws!  I see that I was one of your 7s, so happy that I was :-) I do like the heavy plating and those hairs on the back over the bands.  This is one of the very few times where I can say that I wouldn''t have minded seeing a little more contrast and a hit of sharpening just to further emphasize that fantastical texture.  The b/w is a good choice as that way the form of the armadillo draws us further in.<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful!<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! What, those things can run? Never would have guessed it, but bet it can dig like hell with those claws!  I see that I was one of your 7s, so happy that I was :-) I do like the heavy plating and those hairs on the back over the bands.  This is one of the very few times where I can say that I wouldn''t have minded seeing a little more contrast and a hit of sharpening just to further emphasize that fantastical texture.  The b/w is a good choice as that way the form of the armadillo draws us further in. Hope this has been helpful! Susan', '2016-02-20 21:14:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7438515, 1175533, 67697, '<td valign="top">I''ve never seen an armadillo prepping for a leap lol. The detail you captured - especially with the fine hairs is great.</td>', 'I''ve never seen an armadillo prepping for a leap lol. The detail you captured - especially with the fine hairs is great.', '2016-02-20 23:21:04.000000', NULL, 0),
